    "91508891-f045-5e80-bec6-b1fc6b74b3f0": {
      "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
      "name": "4. Aurora appears twice",
      "visible": true,
      "parameters": {
        "zoom": 7.65,
        "extent": [
          7514065.63,
          3061141.04,
          9072538.5,
          3829123.84
        ],
        "enableIdentify": true,
        "content": {
          "contentMode": "map",
          "markdown": "<div style='font-size:18px; line-height:1.55; min-height:84vh;'><div style='font-size:14px; color:#64748b; letter-spacing:.03em; margin:0 0 8px;'>2 · System · Weather: Aurora 1.5 · Pollutants: synthetic (CAMS needs an account)</div><ol style='margin:0 0 10px 22px; padding:0;'><li style='margin:0 0 5px;'><b>Inputs</b> · CAMS global analysis 0.4° (PM, NO2, SO2, O3, CO + meteorology) · ERA5 or IFS HRES T0 0.25° (26 surface variables, 13 levels)</li><li style='margin:0 0 5px;'><b>Aurora 0.4° Air Pollution</b> · 12 h × 4 = 48 h. Local GPU or the Foundry \"Aurora\" endpoint</li><li style='margin:0 0 5px;'><b>Aurora 1.5</b> · 6 h × 8 + hourly sub-steps = 48 hourly fields (boundary-layer height, 10 m wind, temperature, dew point, rain, gusts)</li><li style='margin:0 0 5px;'><b>Delhi post-processing</b> · 10-site interpolation → CPCB AQI → GRAP stage → stagnation (wind &lt; 10 km/h, mixing height &lt; 500 m) → hi/en/ko messages → push, SMS, WhatsApp, app</li></ol><p style='margin:0 0 10px;'><b>Why two models.</b> Aurora 1.5 is weather-only and predicts no pollutants, but gives <b>hourly</b> dispersion conditions. The Air Pollution model predicts concentrations directly, at 12-hour steps and 0.4°. Together they answer \"how high\" and \"from what hour tonight\".</p><p style='margin:0 0 10px;'><b>What \"high resolution\" means.</b> (1) Time: hourly from 1.5 with <code style='background:rgba(100,116,139,.18); padding:0 4px; border-radius:4px; font-size:.92em;'>fine_lead_times=[1,…,6]</code>. (2) Space: the thin grid on the map is 1.5's 0.25° cells, bilinearly interpolated to ten sites. The grid itself cannot resolve intra-city differences (§6).</p><p style='margin:0 0 10px;'><b>Linkages.</b> The repository's <code style='background:rgba(100,116,139,.18); padding:0 4px; border-radius:4px; font-size:.92em;'>msresearch-aurora/</code> (the Aurora skill from microsoft/vibe-kit) supplies a React map frontend, validation utilities and a fine-tuning starter. Checkpoints come from HuggingFace <code style='background:rgba(100,116,139,.18); padding:0 4px; border-radius:4px; font-size:.92em;'>microsoft/aurora</code>; without a GPU, <code style='background:rgba(100,116,139,.18); padding:0 4px; border-radius:4px; font-size:.92em;'>--mode foundry</code> submits to the Azure AI Foundry \"Aurora\" and \"Aurora-1.5\" endpoints.</p></div>",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "50%"
        },
        "transition": {
          "type": "smooth",
          "time": 2.0
