        "content": {
          "contentMode": "map",
          "markdown": "<div style='font-size:18px; line-height:1.55; min-height:84vh;'><div style='font-size:14px; color:#64748b; letter-spacing:.03em; margin:0 0 8px;'>3 · S6 · Weather: Aurora 1.5 · Additional method</div><p style='margin:0 0 10px;'>For the first night (5 Nov 22:00 to 6 Nov 08:00) Aurora 1.5 puts Anand Vihar's mixing layer as low as 137 m with a median wind of 11.1 km/h; the short lines on the map are that wind (from the cell centre toward where the air moves, length by speed). With the same emissions and a thinner layer of air to mix into, surface concentrations rise. The message says \"pollution will tend to pool near the surface from night to morning\", and sensitive groups can get a reminder to close windows and skip early exercise.</p></div>",
