    "f5bf1ab1-7652-5f51-8080-697800cfd3e4": {
      "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
      "name": "9. 7 Nov 05:30 IST, the worst-hit site",
      "visible": true,
      "parameters": {
        "zoom": 12.1,
        "extent": [
          8552676.48,
          3312159.86,
          8623920.95,
          3345134.73
        ],
        "enableIdentify": true,
        "content": {
          "contentMode": "map",
          "markdown": "<div style='font-size:18px; line-height:1.55; min-height:84vh;'><div style='font-size:14px; color:#64748b; letter-spacing:.03em; margin:0 0 8px;'>3 · S7 · Weather: Aurora 1.5 · Pollutants: synthetic (CAMS needs an account) · Additional method</div><p style='margin:0 0 10px;'>The second pre-dawn. Anand Vihar in east Delhi (a traffic site where an interstate bus terminal meets arterial roads) reaches AQI 500 (Severe); neighbouring ITO, Noida and Okhla exceed 450. This hour becomes the \"peak time\" in the per-site summary, and the 06:00 IST morning update sends \"peak 07:00–09:00, wear a mask\" before school and commute.</p><p style='margin:0 0 10px;'><b>Operator long message · Anand Vihar</b></p><pre style='font-size:15px; line-height:1.45; white-space:pre-wrap; background:rgba(100,116,139,.12); padding:8px 11px; border-radius:8px; margin:6px 0 10px;'>- AQI now 385, peaking at 500 (Severe) around 07 Nov 05:30 IST. Trend: roughly steady.\n- Main pollutant: PM10. PM2.5 up to 321 ug/m3, PM10 up to 514 ug/m3.\n- Dispersion: Stagnant conditions (wind below 10 km/h, mixing height below 500 m) are expected for 12 h, 2 h of them overnight (minimum mixing height about 67 m). Pollution will tend to pool near the surface from night to morning.\n- Health advice: Even healthy people are affected. Stay indoors as much as possible; children, older adults and people with lung or heart disease should avoid going out. Use an air purifier and seek medical care if symptoms appear.\n- Measures: GRAP Stage IV (Severe+) level: truck entry restrictions, expanded work-from-home and online classes may be enforced. Follow official notices.\n- This is AI-model (Aurora) guidance for information only; follow official CPCB/CAQM alerts.</pre></div>",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "50%"
        },
