          "markdown": "<div style='font-size:18px; line-height:1.55; min-height:84vh;'><div style='font-size:14px; color:#64748b; letter-spacing:.03em; margin:0 0 8px;'>3 · S6 · afternoon · Weather: Aurora 1.5 · Pollutants: synthetic (CAMS needs an account)</div><p style='margin:0 0 10px;'>For a few hours the mixing layer climbs toward 1,000 m, winds exceed 10 km/h and the AQI dips below 400. It is still \"Very Poor\". This is the window in which sensitive groups can ventilate or go out, and the message names it. Afterwards (S8) per-site predictions are compared with CPCB/DPCC observations to derive bias corrections.</p></div>",
