    "cbe121fe-e65d-5426-b726-de7e93c78357": {
      "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
      "name": "13. The truth about resolution",
      "visible": true,
      "parameters": {
        "zoom": 10.46,
        "extent": [
          8421319.48,
          3274212.69,
          8643958.46,
          3382011.46
        ],
        "enableIdentify": true,
        "content": {
          "contentMode": "map",
          "markdown": "<div style='font-size:18px; line-height:1.55; min-height:84vh;'><div style='font-size:14px; color:#64748b; letter-spacing:.03em; margin:0 0 8px;'>6 · Limits and responsible use · Pollutants: synthetic (CAMS needs an account)</div><p style='margin:0 0 10px;'>The large square on the map is one 0.4° cell of the Air Pollution model. All of Delhi NCT fits in two or three cells.</p><ul style='margin:0 0 10px 22px; padding:0;'><li style='margin:0 0 5px;'><b>Spatial resolution</b>: site differences are interpolation, not roadside values. A real service needs per-station bias correction or fine-tuning on CPCB data.</li><li style='margin:0 0 5px;'><b>Temporal resolution</b>: the hourly curve is a linear interpolation of 12-hour forecasts; the hourly structure comes from 1.5's meteorology and the messages say so.</li><li style='margin:0 0 5px;'><b>Input data</b>: 1.5 was fine-tuned on IFS HRES T0; this example uses ERA5. The Air Pollution model is for CAMS analysis only.</li><li style='margin:0 0 5px;'><b>Gases at 1000 hPa</b>: NO2/SO2/O3/CO are converted mixing ratios, an approximation; PM2.5/PM10 dominate the AQI.</li><li style='margin:0 0 5px;'><b>Operational decisions</b>: Aurora is a research model and must not drive operational decisions without expert review.</li></ul></div>",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "50%"
        },
        "transition": {
          "type": "smooth",
          "time": 2.0
        },
        "layerOverride": [
