    "b564f209-1f69-5393-8d4e-0227389eb8a1": {
      "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
      "name": "19. Done and still to do",
      "visible": true,
      "parameters": {
        "zoom": 7.65,
        "extent": [
          7514065.63,
          3061141.04,
          9072538.5,
          3829123.84
        ],
        "enableIdentify": true,
        "content": {
          "contentMode": "map",
          "markdown": "<div style='font-size:18px; line-height:1.55; min-height:84vh;'><div style='font-size:14px; color:#64748b; letter-spacing:.03em; margin:0 0 8px;'>7 · What remains · run it</div><p style='margin:0 0 10px;'>The five roadmap items were run in the scenes above. What remains: connecting real CPCB observations, the actual fine-tuning on regional data, and attaching a CAMS account so pollutant concentrations also come from Aurora.</p><ol style='margin:0 0 10px 22px; padding:0;'><li style='margin:0 0 5px;'><b>Uncertainty</b>: <code style='background:rgba(100,116,139,.18); padding:0 4px; border-radius:4px; font-size:.92em;'>AuroraV1p5Ensemble</code> with <code style='background:rgba(100,116,139,.18); padding:0 4px; border-radius:4px; font-size:.92em;'>rollout_ensemble</code> for \"80% chance of stagnation\".</li><li style='margin:0 0 5px;'><b>CPCB correction</b>: learn per-site residuals (linear or quantile mapping first).</li><li style='margin:0 0 5px;'><b>Fine-tuning</b>: adapt the Air Pollution model to regional data with the loop in <code style='background:rgba(100,116,139,.18); padding:0 4px; border-radius:4px; font-size:.92em;'>msresearch-aurora/starter-code/</code>; model-side requirements in <code style='background:rgba(100,116,139,.18); padding:0 4px; border-radius:4px; font-size:.92em;'>docs/finetuning.md</code>.</li><li style='margin:0 0 5px;'><b>Channels</b>: push <code style='background:rgba(100,116,139,.18); padding:0 4px; border-radius:4px; font-size:.92em;'>messages_hi.json</code> to the WhatsApp Business API, SMS or the Delhi government app; map users to the nearest site by pin code.</li><li style='margin:0 0 5px;'><b>Automation</b>: cron <code style='background:rgba(100,116,139,.18); padding:0 4px; border-radius:4px; font-size:.92em;'>delhi_aq.py --mode foundry --plot</code> at 00 and 12 UTC.</li></ol><h3 style='font-size:20px; margin:12px 0 6px;'>Run it yourself</h3><p style='margin:0 0 10px;'>Demo mode needs no GPU or data.</p><pre style='font-size:15px; line-height:1.45; white-space:pre-wrap; background:rgba(100,116,139,.12); padding:8px 11px; border-radius:8px; margin:6px 0 10px;'>git clone https://github.com/playground-for-thinker/aurora.git &amp;&amp; cd aurora\npip install -e . &amp;&amp; pip install matplotlib\npython examples/delhi_air_quality/delhi_aq.py --mode demo --date 2025-11-05 --plot --out outputs</pre><ul style='margin:0 0 10px 22px; padding:0;'><li style='margin:0 0 5px;'>Notebook: <a href='https://colab.research.google.com/github/playground-for-thinker/aurora/blob/main/examples/delhi_air_quality/example_delhi_air_quality.ipynb'>Colab</a> · <a href='https://mybinder.org/v2/gh/playground-for-thinker/aurora/main?labpath=examples%2Fdelhi_air_quality%2Fexample_delhi_air_quality.ipynb'>Binder</a></li><li style='margin:0 0 5px;'>Storyboard (scene-by-scene document with charts, notebook.link): <a href='https://notebook.link/github/playground-for-thinker/aurora/tree/storymap/specta/?path=storyboard_en.ipynb'>English</a> · <a href='https://notebook.link/github/playground-for-thinker/aurora/tree/storymap/specta/?path=storyboard_ko.ipynb'>Korean</a></li><li style='margin:0 0 5px;'>Code: <a href='https://github.com/playground-for-thinker/aurora/tree/main/examples/delhi_air_quality'>GitHub</a></li></ul><p style='margin:0 0 10px;'>This story map is a JupyterGIS document (<code style='background:rgba(100,116,139,.18); padding:0 4px; border-radius:4px; font-size:.92em;'>.jGIS</code>). Open it in notebook.link's JupyterLab view to edit layers and scenes, or rebuild it from pipeline outputs with <code style='background:rgba(100,116,139,.18); padding:0 4px; border-radius:4px; font-size:.92em;'>build_storymap_jgis.py</code>.</p></div>",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "paneAlignment": "start",
          "panelWidth": "50%"
        },
        "transition": {
          "type": "smooth",
          "time": 2.0
        },
